Cheats: what came from where
============================

gpsp/cheat_engine.c, cheat_engine_tables.h
    Ported from mGBA (https://github.com/mgba-emu/mgba, commit c3c8e5e,
    MPL-2.0, Copyright (c) 2013-2016 Jeffrey Pfau):
      src/gba/cheats/codebreaker.c   CodeBreaker decoding and cipher
      src/gba/cheats/gameshark.c     GameShark Advance / Action Replay v1-v2,
                                     TEA, seed tables (verbatim)
      src/gba/cheats/parv3.c         Pro Action Replay v3, seed tables
      src/gba/cheats.c               GBACheatAddressIsReal, autodetection
      src/core/cheats.c              the interpreter loop (mCheatRefresh)
      src/gb/cheats.c                Game Boy GameShark / Game Genie
    Changes are marked "GBAdhoc:" in the source.  The CodeBreaker button and
    add-32 forms follow gpSP's own cheats.c (VBA-M semantics); the Game
    Genie's 15-bit address compare follows Gambatte.

gpsp/vita/tests/cheats/mgba/gba_test_cheats.c
    mGBA src/gba/test/cheats.c, unmodified (MPL-2.0).

gpsp/vita/tests/cheats/vbam_ref.cpp
    Unmodified excerpts of VisualBoyAdvance-M src/core/gba/gbaCheats.cpp
    (https://github.com/visualboyadvance-m/visualboyadvance-m, commit
    6fe6bb4, GPL-2.0-or-later): the reference the ciphers are tested
    against.  Test only; not in the app.

gpsp/vita/assets/cheats.db
    Built by tools/make_cheatdb.py from libretro-database
    (https://github.com/libretro/libretro-database, commit d5bae90):
    cht/Nintendo - Game Boy Advance, - Game Boy, - Game Boy Color, and
    metadat/no-intro/Nintendo - Game Boy*.dat (names, CRC-32, serials).
    assets/cheats.db.txt is that build's report.
